    "/apis/v1/firms-modaps-eosdis-nasa-gov/wildfire-detections/records-list": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Collect every current detection of a sensor for a window and region; walk regions instead of Global to keep 7d files small.",
        "operationId": "firms-modaps-eosdis-nasa-gov.wildfire-detections.records-list",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "properties": {
                  "cursor": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "`next_cursor` from the previous page. Omit for the first page; a cursor from another file or sensor is rejected.",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body"
                    }
                  },
                  "limit": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Maximum rows per page. Rows left in the fetched byte range are re-read on the next page.\n\nProvider reference: minimum 1; maximum 50000; default 1000.",
                    "default": 1000,
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": 1,
                      "max": 50000
                    }
                  },
                  "page_bytes": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Bytes fetched per page (one Range request). Default 4 MiB.\n\nProvider reference: minimum 65536; maximum 8388608; default 4194304.",
                    "default": 4194304,
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "min": 65536,
                      "max": 8388608
                    }
                  },
                  "region": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Default Global. landsat only publishes Canada and USA_contiguous_and_Hawaii.\n\nProvider reference: allowed values [\"Global\", \"Canada\", \"Alaska\", \"USA_contiguous_and_Hawaii\", \"Central_America\", \"South_America\", \"Europe\", \"Northern_and_Central_Africa\", \"Southern_Africa\", \"Russia_Asia\", \"South_Asia\", \"SouthEast_Asia\", \"Australia_NewZealand\"]; default \"Global\".",
                    "default": "Global",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body",
                      "oneOf": [
                        "Global",
                        "Canada",
                        "Alaska",
                        "USA_contiguous_and_Hawaii",
                        "Central_America",
                        "South_America",
                        "Europe",
                        "Northern_and_Central_Africa",
                        "Southern_Africa",
                        "Russia_Asia",
                        "South_Asia",
                        "SouthEast_Asia",
                        "Australia_NewZealand"
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  "sensor": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "sensor\n\nProvider reference: allowed values [\"suomi-npp-viirs-c2\", \"noaa-20-viirs-c2\", \"noaa-21-viirs-c2\", \"modis-c6.1\", \"landsat\"]."
                  },
                  "summary_only": {
                    "type": "boolean",
                    "description": "Count the rows of the page without returning them (records is empty).",
                    "x-alexandria-option-metadata": {
                      "in": "body"
                    }
                  },
                  "window": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "window\n\nProvider reference: allowed values [\"24h\", \"48h\", \"7d\"]."
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "sensor",
                  "window"
                ]
              },
              "examples": {
                "provider": {
                  "summary": "Official provider example; checked against AIsa request constraints",
                  "value": {
                    "limit": 2,
                    "page_bytes": 65536,
                    "region": "Northern_and_Central_Africa",
                    "sensor": "noaa-20-viirs-c2",
                    "window": "24h"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The detections of one keyless active-fire CSV file (segment = sensor x window x region), paged by byte range and pinned to one publication. Each page fetches one `Range` of the file, trims to whole lines and returns up to `limit` rows; the cursor carries the file's ETag and SHA-256 plus the next byte offset, and a page whose ETag no longer matches fails with invalid_input issue code `publication_changed` instead of mixing versions. When one page covers the whole file its SHA-256 is verified against x-amz-meta-sha256.\n\nThe response contains the tool result directly.\n\nThe provider identifies `records` as the primary payload key.\n\n| Documented field | Provider type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `acq_date` | string | Acquisition date, UTC. |\n| `acq_time` | string | Acquisition time of the overpass, UTC HHMM, as published. |\n| `acquired_at` | string | acq_date and acq_time combined into an ISO-8601 UTC instant. |\n| `bright_t31` | number | MODIS channel 31 brightness temperature, Kelvin. |\n| `bright_ti4` | number | VIIRS I-4 channel brightness temperature, Kelvin. |\n| `bright_ti5` | number | VIIRS I-5 channel brightness temperature, Kelvin. |\n| `brightness` | number | MODIS channel 21/22 brightness temperature, Kelvin. |\n| `confidence` | string | As published: low/nominal/high (VIIRS, and l/n/h in the area API), 0-100 (MODIS), low/medium/high (Landsat). |\n| `daynight` | string | D or N. |\n| `extra` | object | Any published column not mapped above (for example `instrument`, `country_id` or `type` from the area API), verbatim as strings. |\n| `frp` | number | Fire radiative power in MW; null when the sensor publishes none (Landsat). |\n| `hazard_type` | string |  |\n| `instrument` | string | Derived from the file family or the API's instrument column. |\n| `latitude` | number |  |\n| `longitude` | number |  |\n| `path` | number | Landsat WRS-2 path. |\n| `publication_id` | string | `<file name>@<x-amz-meta-sha256>` of the file the row came from; for the keyed area API `area:<source>:<area>:<day_range>[:<date>]@<retrieved_at>` because the API has no version. |\n| `retrieved_at` | string | UTC ISO-8601 time of the upstream fetch. |\n| `row` | number | Landsat WRS-2 row. |\n| `satellite` | string | N (Suomi NPP), N20 (NOAA-20), N21 (NOAA-21), T (Terra), A (Aqua), L8/L9 (Landsat) as published. |\n| `scan` | number |  |\n| `source_record_id` | string | `<satellite>:<acq_date>T<acq_time>:<latitude>,<longitude>` built from the row's own values (FIRMS publishes no detection id). |\n| `source_url` | string | The file or API URL this row was read from. |\n| `track` | number |  |\n| `version` | string | Product version such as 2.0NRT or 6.1NRT; null for Landsat files, which publish none. |\n\n\nThese are the provider's documented fields. Field requiredness, nullability and nested object structures are specified only where the descriptions explicitly say so.",
